RATBOX [males females] [n]
  A box of pet rats: a swarm on one model (RATBOX.MDL), a LUN a rat -
  each its own habits. RAT decides for each: eat, sleep, play, TV,
  wander, groom a friend, mate, fight a rival, nurse its babies. They
  like or dislike each other. Two males after one female fight in the
  boxing ring (bottom middle). Babies are born in the pen (right side),
  fed by their mother until weaned, bred from their parents' LUNs. The
  dead go to the graveyard (left side). Crowded (over 20): more mess,
  more food, illness, fights, fewer babies.
    RUN 2 MODEL RATBOX : RUN 3 RAT : RATBOX 5 5
  RATBOX alone: the box as saved (RATBOX.SAV), else it asks how many.
  F fill the bowl  T TV  C clean  M medicine (the ill ones)
  . , the next / last rat (@: its state on line 2)
  N the chosen rat to the naughty bed (top middle; less of what it did)
  + praise  - scold (what it is doing: more / less)  Q quit (saved)
